# platform, CI, deploy, web and architecture), and @SpeedyV5 (data, features, prediction,
# club news and the LLM adapter). The zones and their reasons are in ownership.md.
#
# The two-person review rule. Ownership means who must approve a change, not exclusive
# access. A change inside one owner's zone needs that owner's approval unless that owner
# wrote it. A change to a shared boundary (the last block) needs both owners: an approving
# review from each owner who did not write it. Outside that block, a line that lists both
# accounts names alternative reviewers and either approval is enough; listing both does not
# make a path a shared boundary. Later rules win, so the shared surfaces come last.
#
# As read on 2026-09-25, branch protection does not require code-owner review, so this file
# requests reviews and does not block a merge; the two owners keep the rule, not the
# settings. docs/architecture/branching.md says how to re-read the settings.
